#!/usr/bin/python3
"""untrash-installer - first-time setup of UntrashOS in the browser.

docs/architecture/installer-plan.md.  Serves http://zyxel-untrash/ (port 80,
or ZT_INSTALLER_PORT).  Four ways:
  A  new install, wipe the selected disk          (COPY key confirmation)
  B  keep the data, take over stock users/shares  (COPY key confirmation)
  C  keep the data, new users/configuration       (COPY key confirmation)
  D  back to the stock firmware from the stick's backup (COPY key; reboot,
     loader RAM mark, stock PartnerKey restores and powers off)

Every destructive run first backs up the partition table and the RAID/LVM
metadata of the affected disk to the stick.  B/C never
repartition: UntrashOS goes as files into /.untrash/ of a stock volume
(slot-a/b.utslot, state.img, swap.img, bootstate); the loader boots from there.  ZT_INSTALLER_DRYRUN=1 only logs
the commands; ZT_INSTALLER_TEST=1 also lists loop devices (self-tests).
"""
